<<~ ahu #/meme-header>>

! Guest Grammar — Extended Docs

This file does not bind invariant law.
Law lives in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/guest-grammar`.
This surface carries examples, ownership notes, and split residue.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ownership-notes>>

!! Ownership Notes

| locus | owns |
|---|---|
| `memetic-wikitext` | primitive cluster, boot surface, distinction between identity payload and local priming payload |
| `guest-grammar` | admission law, hana worksite law, host-guest distinction |
| parser | guest entry recognition, legality, local warning behavior |
| render-pipeline | lowering, projection, landing |
| pono | law indexing, packaging, later verification support |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/fixture-seeds>>

!! Fixture Seeds

The first fixture family should include:

* one clean `hana` block with `x-tiddlywiki-filter`
* one malformed priming payload
* one malformed guest body with recoverable host structure
* one null-context `+currentMeme` case
* one trace continuity case from surface to AST to widget to output
* one anti-overload case showing that root primitives remain distinct from guest work

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/admission-notes>>

!! Admission Notes

A lawful admission should keep these distinctions visible:

* explicit host entry versus ambient punctuation
* canonical meme identity versus local priming payload
* host primitive family versus guest invocation family
* degraded guest region versus parent collapse

When a region needs long legality tables, schema detail, or runtime procedure, move that material outward instead of re-expanding the parent.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/migration-note>>

!! Migration Note

This docs companion formed during the 2026-04-21 yin split/refine/clean pass.
The old parent mixed invariant law, ownership tables, canonical forms, degradation detail, lowering handoff, and fixture seeds.
The current shape keeps:

* parent invariant at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/guest-grammar`
* operational procedure at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/guest-grammar/SKILL`
* extended guidance here

<<~/ahu>>

